{"id":167052689,"slug":"why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as","title":"Why Isn't Beck's \"Colors\" Heralded as the Most Important Party Rock Album Ever?","subtitle":"It's a damn masterpiece.","post_date":"2025-06-29T14:13:10.240Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as","wordcount":758,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:47:00.047Z","body_sha256":"5da0424e9e170f35a4d28a05a50432afacc3d69dc00d250a99dd0bbae488c5b1","text_words":758,"complete":true,"body_html":"<div class=\"pullquote\"><p>Dear life, I’m holding on<br>How long must I wait<br>Before the thrill is gone</p><p>—Beck, “<a href=\"https://genius.com/Beck-dear-life-lyrics\">Dear Life</a>”</p></div><p>Party Rock—it’s an underrated genre.  Sure, these kinds of songs can be pilloried as Yacht Rock:</p><blockquote><p><em>subgenre of soft rock, popular in the late 1970s and early 1980s, characterized by its smooth, mellow sound, often evoking images of sailing or cruising on a yacht</em></p></blockquote><p>But when you are throwing a rocking party—or simply need to get your day started—it can’t always be <a href=\"https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/music/story/2024-01-04/ratm-rage-against-the-machine-not-touring-again-drummer-brad-wilk\">Rage Against the Machine.</a></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"743\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:743,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:2116874,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/167052689?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yZAe!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F01a08d85-83f0-435f-9233-db1521503294_1818x928.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Sometimes, you need to get the party started, but <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MUaL1FnotRQ\">not explain more to your children </a>than you have energy to support.</p><p>That is where I find myself today.  I want to get the party started.  I have some excellent choices when it comes to individual songs.  No, I’m not talking about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Party_Rock_Anthem\">Party Rock Anthem.</a>  No, I’m not referring to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitbull_(rapper)\">Pitbull</a>.  I’m looking to get the party started, but in a way that will involve minimal cringe-induction.</p><p>I could always listen to Modest Mouse.  OF COURSE, I could listen to Modest Mouse.  <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/neuromodulation-via-modest-mouse?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">I’ve been doing that since 1997.</a>  Readers of this newsletter who are fans of all things Owen could even <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/0h2ENRw6OxwFuSpMXCxbp7?si=8hzadjgUTCqMO597mU6X6A\">listen to some of my music.</a>  It’s not great party music, though.  If you want to have a really navel-gazing party, one could listen to <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/american-football?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">American Football</a>.</p><p>Yes, this newsletter is a stealth music newsletter.  I get that.  We have a whole series of articles comparing hip-hop classics to portions of the rules around mental health parity.</p><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;d07b8b17-a849-43c8-9eee-f00bf32572db&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Welcome to the leading source of hip-hop-related regulatory guidance from your Beloved OpenCommentOutsider.com. The tunes you love and guidance for federal regulators! This series about mental health parity intends to get you, dear readers, to email the Department of Labor and request they do things right.&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;sm&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Thrift Shop: How Narrow Networks With High Quality Can Win Mental Health Parity...&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2023-07-31T13:01:50.230Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/youtube/w_728,c_limit/QK8mJJJvaes&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/thrift-shop-how-narrow-networks-with&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:135570144,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:4,&quot;comment_count&quot;:1,&quot;publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;0c353910-1cfe-4adf-a89d-00ed0586767b&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Readers of this newsletter know I have one true love: Open Comment Periods on Regulations.gov. Additionally, I enjoy using R+B to make points about regulatory matters. We need to act. Please subscribe and share while we are at it….&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;sm&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Say My Name: The Department of Labor &amp; Destiny's Child Have In Common--CHEATERS WILL BE CALLED OUT!&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2023-07-26T18:52:54.136Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/youtube/w_728,c_limit/sQgd6MccwZc&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/say-my-name-the-department-of-labor&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:135470905,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:2,&quot;comment_count&quot;:0,&quot;publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;41053af3-eedd-45ba-a1de-c78c452c9f0a&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;This is the second in a many-part series on mental health parity, the MPHAEA enforcement, and the Department of Labor’s new open comment period! Check out Regulations.gov, and feel free to leave an open comment on the proposed rules!&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;sm&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Mental Health Parity: What do Shaggy and Big Insurance Have in Common?&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2023-07-27T19:24:00.658Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/youtube/w_728,c_limit/T_x6QmuJdms&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/mental-health-parity-what-do-shaggy&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:135494239,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:9,&quot;comment_count&quot;:2,&quot;publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><p>And among my favorite articles of all time:</p><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;1e188b0c-a50a-49e9-ab6f-4e126025be81&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Previously, in this newsletter’s series on a request by the Department of Labor to have more robust reporting about mental health parity we learned new things!&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;md&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;No Scrubs: TLC has advice about Mental Health Parity enforcement for the DOL&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2023-07-29T23:16:44.663Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Fbyf!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbf84e1aa-182a-4309-834e-be08a202b01d_1290x1082.jpeg&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/no-scrubs-tlc-has-advice-about-mental&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:135520531,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:7,&quot;comment_count&quot;:0,&quot;publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><p>Now, returning to my point: </p><p>If you want to get the party started, and it is not Christmas, in which case Sufjan Stevens has you covered, and it’s crucially important to keep your “I like good music” credibility intact…I have a solution for you.</p><p>For the life of me, I can’t understand why this remarkable record— <em>Colors</em> by Beck—Is my choice to save both your party and <em>your sense of yourself</em> as having good taste in music.</p><p>The brilliance of <em>Colors</em>—11 sublimely upbeat songs—is that they both get the party started…and don’t suck.  Beck is responsible for some of the most sublime music of the last 30 years.  <em>Sea Change’s</em> “<a href=\"https://youtu.be/EnkaIEfealU?feature=shared\">Paper Tiger</a>,” anyone?  But much of it is mournful or absurdist.  Colors is <em>neither</em>—while still asking serious questions in its lyrics.</p><p>Take “<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Eema4I1KitE\">No Distraction</a>”…a funky love song that also, effortlessly, reminds us— distractions that pull lovers out of the moment are <em>bad</em>:</p><div class=\"pullquote\"><p>It’s not the words I want to tell you<br>It’s not the tension that I feel<br>It’s not the face that I’m showing you today<br>That betrays the way, the way I want to feel<br><br>What I need<br>What I need<br>What I need right now is right here<a href=\"https://genius.com/12900980/Beck-no-distraction/What-i-need-right-now-is-right-here-right-in-front-of-me\"><br></a>Right in front of me<br><br>What I need<br>What I need<br>What I need right now is right here<br>Only you and me.</p></div><div id=\"youtube2-Eema4I1KitE\" class=\"youtube-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;videoId&quot;:&quot;Eema4I1KitE&quot;,&quot;startTime&quot;:null,&quot;endTime&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"Youtube2ToDOM\"><div class=\"youtube-inner\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Eema4I1KitE?rel=0&amp;autoplay=0&amp;showinfo=0&amp;enablejsapi=0\" frameborder=\"0\" loading=\"lazy\" gesture=\"media\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen\" allowautoplay=\"true\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" width=\"728\" height=\"409\"></iframe></div></div><p>Distractions are a giant slapping movement to that phone in both of your hands, and gets you to wiggle your hips enough to make it plausible that you might just be forced to put them down while you both shimmy.  </p><p>How does Beck make colors bounce so hard?  The old-fashioned way—with excellent musicians playing actual music…here is a partial list of the talent on the record:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png\" width=\"408\" height=\"584.5970149253732\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1344,&quot;width&quot;:938,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:408,&quot;bytes&quot;:249177,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/167052689?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Rk3a!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2ab72305-0f85-4b9d-b9bb-4844f9039562_938x1344.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Yes, they had two more double bass players, but I ran out of room on the screenshot.  And Greg Kurstin?  He also co-produces many of the tracks.  Legendary mastering engineers, including <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emily_Lazar\">Emily Lazar</a> (who won a Grammy for this record) and Tom Coyne (whose mastering suite I have spent a non-zero amount of time in), also polished it up at the end.  This is an album of actual music created by actual musicians, and it shows.  Beck Hanson did the string arrangements himself!</p><p>What makes Colors great?  Great musicians, with well-arranged music, singing and playing well-crafted music, with instruments that move air and analog signals, breathing life into lyrics that are about our lives, with a timelessness that’s hard to ignore.</p><p>Take that, synth pop.  </p><div class=\"captioned-button-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CaptionedButtonToDOM\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading The Frontier Psychiatrists ! This post is public, so feel free to share it.</p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p></div><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><div><hr></div><p>Thanks for joining me on this Sunday musical excursion.  If you—or someone you know— needs the most advanced mental health care?  That is an option, across 18 states by telemedicine, and with our in-person interventional centers in 3 states <em>already</em>.   Yep, it’s my day job, <strong>Radial</strong>.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.meetradial.com&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Explore Care at Radial&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://www.meetradial.com\"><span>Explore Care at Radial</span></a></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p></p><p> </p>","text":"Dear life, I’m holding on\nHow long must I wait\nBefore the thrill is gone\n\n—Beck, “ Dear Life ”\n\nParty Rock—it’s an underrated genre. Sure, these kinds of songs can be pilloried as Yacht Rock:\n\nsubgenre of soft rock, popular in the late 1970s and early 1980s, characterized by its smooth, mellow sound, often evoking images of sailing or cruising on a yacht\n\nBut when you are throwing a rocking party—or simply need to get your day started—it can’t always be Rage Against the Machine.\n\nShare\n\nSometimes, you need to get the party started, but not explain more to your children than you have energy to support.\n\nThat is where I find myself today. I want to get the party started. I have some excellent choices when it comes to individual songs. No, I’m not talking about Party Rock Anthem. No, I’m not referring to Pitbull . I’m looking to get the party started, but in a way that will involve minimal cringe-induction.\n\nI could always listen to Modest Mouse. OF COURSE, I could listen to Modest Mouse. I’ve been doing that since 1997. Readers of this newsletter who are fans of all things Owen could even listen to some of my music. It’s not great party music, though. If you want to have a really navel-gazing party, one could listen to American Football .\n\nYes, this newsletter is a stealth music newsletter. I get that. We have a whole series of articles comparing hip-hop classics to portions of the rules around mental health parity.\n\nAnd among my favorite articles of all time:\n\nNow, returning to my point:\n\nIf you want to get the party started, and it is not Christmas, in which case Sufjan Stevens has you covered, and it’s crucially important to keep your “I like good music” credibility intact…I have a solution for you.\n\nFor the life of me, I can’t understand why this remarkable record— Colors by Beck—Is my choice to save both your party and your sense of yourself as having good taste in music.\n\nThe brilliance of Colors —11 sublimely upbeat songs—is that they both get the party started…and don’t suck. Beck is responsible for some of the most sublime music of the last 30 years. Sea Change’s “ Paper Tiger ,” anyone? But much of it is mournful or absurdist. Colors is neither —while still asking serious questions in its lyrics.\n\nTake “ No Distraction ”…a funky love song that also, effortlessly, reminds us— distractions that pull lovers out of the moment are bad :\n\nIt’s not the words I want to tell you\nIt’s not the tension that I feel\nIt’s not the face that I’m showing you today\nThat betrays the way, the way I want to feel\n\nWhat I need\nWhat I need\nWhat I need right now is right here\nRight in front of me\n\nWhat I need\nWhat I need\nWhat I need right now is right here\nOnly you and me.\n\nDistractions are a giant slapping movement to that phone in both of your hands, and gets you to wiggle your hips enough to make it plausible that you might just be forced to put them down while you both shimmy.\n\nHow does Beck make colors bounce so hard? The old-fashioned way—with excellent musicians playing actual music…here is a partial list of the talent on the record:\n\nYes, they had two more double bass players, but I ran out of room on the screenshot. And Greg Kurstin? He also co-produces many of the tracks. Legendary mastering engineers, including Emily Lazar (who won a Grammy for this record) and Tom Coyne (whose mastering suite I have spent a non-zero amount of time in), also polished it up at the end. This is an album of actual music created by actual musicians, and it shows. Beck Hanson did the string arrangements himself!\n\nWhat makes Colors great? Great musicians, with well-arranged music, singing and playing well-crafted music, with instruments that move air and analog signals, breathing life into lyrics that are about our lives, with a timelessness that’s hard to ignore.\n\nTake that, synth pop.\n\nThanks for reading The Frontier Psychiatrists ! This post is public, so feel free to share it.\n\nShare\n\nSubscribe now\n\nThanks for joining me on this Sunday musical excursion. If you—or someone you know— needs the most advanced mental health care? That is an option, across 18 states by telemedicine, and with our in-person interventional centers in 3 states already . Yep, it’s my day job, Radial .\n\nExplore Care at Radial"}